    "body": "I noticed on windows when trying to browse a file share using a UNC path (//server/share or \\\\server\\share) the leading slash was eaten as part of the file normalization. \r\n\r\nThis PR modifies the windows normalization function on windows to allow two leading slashes, but otherwise remove any repeats.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-09-16T12:50:53Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nLooks reasonable. As I don't have easy access to a Windows machine, I'll double check: does this indeed solve the use case described here? I.e. did you specifically check with these changes?",
