        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@echasnovski Thanks for looking at this!\r\n\r\nYes, I've tested it accessing file shares on windows, it's my main OS.\r\n\r\nI tried to browse files on a home assistant config share and couldn't - when I tried I got a ```'path' is not a valid path``` error which showed the path with a missing slash. After applying this change to a local copy of mini in Lazy.vim, it works fine. \r\n\r\nThe other bits of windows file normalization don't seem to cause any issues.",
